cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Bulwark: agent security posture management for MCP and AI agents"
message: "If you use Bulwark in research or a security assessment, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Abdul
    family-names: Manan
    alias: abdulmanan69
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdulmanan69/bulwark"
url: "https://github.com/abdulmanan69/bulwark"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  Bulwark inventories the attack surface reachable by AI coding agents -- MCP
  servers, tool descriptions, hooks, permission rules, skills and persistent
  instruction files -- and detects prompt injection in tool descriptions,
  Unicode-smuggled payloads, post-review definition changes (rug pulls),
  supply-chain weaknesses, excessive agency, and the combination of private
  data access, untrusted input and outbound egress in a single agent. It pins
  reviewed tool definitions to a lockfile and enforces that pin at runtime
  through an MCP proxy.
keywords:
  - security
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - ai-security
  - llm-security
  - prompt-injection
  - tool-poisoning
  - supply-chain-security
  - agent-security
  - sarif
  - cyclonedx
  - aibom
